      "id": 210167,
      "name": "Christopher",
      "username": "Christopher",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/christopher/{size}/1851_2.png",
      "created_at": "2017-12-05T13:51:57.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>The min, mid, or max dice being referenced by those twists don't come from the environment - they specifically mean the dice that were just rolled by the hero.&nbsp;</p><p>So, if a hero rolls a 3, 4, and 5 on an Overcome, the mid result is 4, which means the Overcome succeeds with a minor twist. So, if you select a minor twist that interacts with the min die, that min die result is 3!</p><p>Does that make sense? Hope it helps!</p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:40:27.732Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
